    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. regarding the testing and staging gates, what are the specific 'red flags' or failure conditions that should trigger an automatic rollback or block a build from moving forward? i want to make sure we're clear on what actually constitutes a 'fail' vs just a warning.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For automatic blocking, failure in unit or integration tests is a critical \"red flag\" and must halt the pipeline immediately. In automated testing, any major functional test failure or critical performance degradation should trigger an immediate block. At the staging gate, observable issues like failed API connections or significant security scan vulnerabilities (e.g., high-severity CVEs) warrant an automatic rollback or build block. Warnings should be logged and reviewed, but only critical failures should trigger an automatic halt.",
      "source": "target",
