      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To catch \"unknown unknowns,\" introduce exploratory testing and chaos engineering into your staging environment. This involves intentionally breaking parts of the system to test resilience, rather than just testing expected flows. Furthermore, implement rigorous real-user monitoring (RUM) in production that watches for unexpected user behavior or unusual latency spikes. These metrics act as a final safety net, flagging problems that traditional automated gates simply cannot anticipate.",
      "source": "target",
